    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive anchor; his score of 80.13 is driven by a favorable matchup against the right-handed Hunter Dobbins and a massive 14% boost from a dynamic platoon edge, further solidified by his leadoff status. Alongside him, **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) and **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) are primary targets, with **Lars Nootbaar** capitalizing on a +10% order bonus and a generous +11% platoon advantage against the right-handed Bryce Elder. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18) remains a high-floor start despite a tough draw against Dean Kremer, as his role at the top of the lineup and an elite xwOBA of 0.373 provide essential stability for our Roto categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (49.77) out of the starting nine. He narrowly missed the cut behind **Colt Keith** (49.13), with the optimizer favoring the latter due to specific positional scarcity and a stronger overall alignment with the projected park factor. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** offers solid peripheral power, his neutral R/R platoon matchup against Freddy Peralta suppressed his efficiency score just enough to keep him as a high-end reserve. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**, both of whom are facing the elite arm of Tarik Skubal. Their scores\u201442.83 and 39.81, respectively\u2014sit near the basement of our active threshold, and with Skubal\u2019s 2.77 xERA, they carry the highest risk in the lineup; should **Gary Sanchez** or **Christian Yelich** be moved down the order upon final lineup confirmation, we may need to pivot to bench depth to protect our daily game caps.",
